[1m[38;5;231mWhat should happen if the target file already exists?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mOverwrite silently (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mRe-running for the same day replaces the file. Idempotent; safe for cron retries.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Refuse unless --force
     [38;5;246mExit non-zero on an existing file. Protects against clobbering, but a cron retry fails.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Overwrite, but atomically
     [38;5;246mWrite to a temp file in the same directory, then rename over the target. No partial file if the write dies.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
